###############################################################################################
#                                         NOTE                                                #
#  1. For the 1st column, you should provide sample id. It is recommended giving the id that  #
#     is consistent with SM tag in BAM header if bam/cram sample.                             #
#  2. For the 2nd column, you should provide sex corresponding to the sample id. The single   #
#     character "F" and "M" represents female and male,	respectively.					      #
#  3. For the 3rd column, you should provide platform info. pb-clr, pb-hifi, ont are allowed. #
#  4. For the 4th column, you should provide the absolute path of sample. Various sample type #
#     are allowed such as fastq, assembly fasta, bam, cram.                                   #
#  5. Mixed input types are allowed.                                                          #
#  6. Non-sample line must be starts with "#".                                                #
#  7. Various file suffix are allowed such as fq, fq.gz, fastq, fastq.gz, fa, fa.gz, fasta,   #
#     fasta.gz, bam, cram.                                                                    #
###############################################################################################

# sample_id	sex	platform	file
# s1	M	pb-clr	s1.fq.gz/s1.fq/s1.fastq/s1.fastq.gz
# s2	M	pb-hifi	s2.bam
# s3	F	pb-hifi	s3.cram
# s4	F	ont	s4.assmb.fa/s4.assmb.fa.gz/s4.assmb.fasta/s4.assmb.fasta.gz
